 "finding": "NO MODEL IN A FAMILY OF 61 FITS EVERY CELL, but the residual is small, ONE-SIDED and structured, which is a usable result rather than a failure. \"premul:round + back:float + out:trunc\" reproduces 1005 of 1024 cells — 98.1 % — and this record's own round(D + a(S-D)) manages 44/256, 45/256, 256/256, 38/256: it is correct ONLY over pure black, where the backdrop term vanishes and every account collapses to the same thing. That is why it survived twenty sections.\n\nTHE RESIDUAL IS A BOUND. All 19 misses are exactly +1 in one or two channels and NONE is -1, so the fitted model never over-predicts: a measured code is the predicted code or one above it. The misses cluster at particular alphas rather than scattering — every multiple of 32 for CYAN over the stage plate (blue only), and 64/128/192 plus 149/213/234 for both pairs over the modal medium (green, with red joining at 128 and 213) — so the exact rule is an integer-arithmetic detail of the reduction stage and not a second mechanism.\n\nSO A PREDICTED TRIPLE IS USABLE AGAIN, WITH A STATED TOLERANCE: predicted by this model, +1/-0 per channel. That is enough for any statement whose margin exceeds one code and NOT enough for A-G139's question, where the three candidate floors span 0.329 to 0.956 q_proj — a spread far larger than one code, and therefore not decidable by a predicted triple at all. §74's rule survives in sharper form: pooled luminances are trustworthy; a predicted triple is trustworthy to +1/-0 and no better."
